==================== SHIM BUGS FIXED BY THIS MEASUREMENT ====================

12 SIGSEGVs in the first ghost-robot run were shim-harness gaps, now closed
(final run: 0 crashes):
  * ZEN_ORACLE_INIT_SCAN — GR fills eb_av1_scan_orders at runtime via
    svt_aom_init_iscan(); a __attribute__((constructor)) in zen_oracle.h runs
    it at load time (hybrid/mainline tables are const).
  * ZEN_ORACLE_REFS_IN_CTX — GR rewrote setup_ref_mv_list into an all-refs
    form writing ctx->ref_mv_stack / xd->ref_mv_count / ctx->inter_mode_ctx.
  * ZEN_ORACLE_EC_PARENT — GR's OdEcEnc borrows its buffer through
    OutputBitstreamUnit (end/buffer_parent); a hand-malloc'd buffer without
    them drops every byte and enc_done returns NULL.
  * pcs->scs wiring — GR reads pcs->scs->subsampling_x (is_dv_valid chroma
    guard) where hybrid reads pcs->ppcs->scs.
  * me_statics — GR's Release build fully inlines hme_level_2 /
    check_00_center; build.rs tries the usual statics promotion, it fails
    (no symbols at all), the cfg stays off and the Rust wrappers return
    None. 4 tests early-return via me_statics_oracle_is_available();
    SVT_CREF_REQUIRE_ME_STATICS=1 makes it loud.

Gates (default hybrid oracle, this commit):
